NAME
       date - print the system date and time

SYNOPSIS
       date [-uRI] [-d @SECONDS] [+FORMAT]

DESCRIPTION
       Display the current time in the given FORMAT. The time zone is set in
       Settings.

OPTIONS
       -u
           print Coordinated Universal Time

       -R
           RFC 5322 format

       -I
           ISO 8601 date

       -d @SECONDS
           display the given Unix time instead of now

       +FORMAT
           strftime format: %Y year, %m month, %d day, %H:%M:%S time, %a/%A
           weekday, %b/%B month name, %s seconds since 1970, %Z zone, %%

EXAMPLES
       date
       date '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M'
       date -d @0 -u

SEE ALSO
       uptime(1)
